Wiren Board kernel config
=========================

Wiren Board 6 and 7 kernel configs are generated by taking an upstream
default config of the SoC family (defconfig in this directory) and applying
a Wiren Board config fragment as overlay, the same way as for Wiren Board 8
(see arch/arm64/configs/README.wb-config):

  Wiren Board 6:  imx_v6_v7_defconfig + wb6.config, wb6-bootlet.config
  Wiren Board 7:  sunxi_defconfig     + wb7.config, wb7-bootlet.config,
                                        wb7-38071cb.config, wb7-som-test.config

Each fragment has two parts: options set by Wiren Board, and options of the
base defconfig that are switched off for Wiren Board.


How to change config?
---------------------

Edit the fragment directly, or use savedefconfig twice to find what you
changed via menuconfig:

```
$ make ARCH=arm sunxi_defconfig wb7.config  # form default config
$ make ARCH=arm savedefconfig  # saves reduced config in this directory
$ mv defconfig defconfig.original

$ make ARCH=arm menuconfig  # do your changes
...
$ make ARCH=arm savedefconfig  # saves new reduced config

$ diff -u defconfig.original defconfig  # analyze this output to change overlay
```


How to build kernel?
--------------------

Wiren Board packaging script is already aware of this overlay thing.
If you want to build your kernel manually, use

```
$ make ARCH=arm imx_v6_v7_defconfig wb6.config
$ make ARCH=arm sunxi_defconfig wb7.config
```
